<article class="env-proposition" id="0BJ8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BJ8">Proposition <span data-tag="0BJ8">33.45.13</span> <span class="named">(Asymptotic Riemann-Roch)</span>.</a>  Let $k$ be a field. Let $X$ be a proper scheme over $k$ of dimension $d$. Let $\mathcal{L}$ be an ample invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \dim _ k \Gamma (X, \mathcal{L}^{\otimes n}) \sim c n^ d + l.o.t.  \]
</div>
  <p> where $c = \deg _\mathcal {L}(X)/d!$ is a positive constant. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the definitions, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BEV" data-tag="0BEV">33.45.9</a>, and the vanishing of higher cohomology in Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0B5U" data-tag="0B5U">30.17.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>